{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"CORRECTION — I have UN-ticked all three ACs I ticked in my previous comment. This ticket is NOT resolved, and the earlier orphan-sweep triage (and my own first pass) was wrong.\n\n'rebar review-plan 514d-a8d8-bb3a-482d' (no --force) returned BLOCK, and its G1G2 finding is CORRECT and I confirmed it independently:\n\nThis ticket's title and Context target the REVIEW BOT's CloudWatch token totals — the follow-up to fd71/clayish-basaltine-bug, whose counts come from _attach_code_review_metrics. What actually landed in bf9fb62a6f ('d52a: thread Pass-1 usage into outputs+sidecar') covers only the PLAN-REVIEW path:\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py sets coverage['usage'], and src/rebar/llm/plan_review/production_batch_runner.py:197 emits outputs['_usage'] — plan-review's ProductionBatchRunner only.\n- The finalize unit test cited as AC2 evidence, tests/unit/workflow/test_pass1_usage.py::test_attach_metrics_folds_token_totals_into_coverage_metrics (line 313), calls _attach_plan_review_metrics — the plan-review assembler, not the code-review one.\n- The CODE-REVIEW finder batch runner, src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py, contains ZERO occurrences of 'usage' — 'grep -n usage src/rebar/llm/code_review/batch_runner.py' returns nothing.\n- src/rebar/llm/code_review/finalize.py:139-141 still documents the gap in the present tense: 'Today that is the Pass-2 verify + Pass-3 decide agent steps — the Pass-1 finder batch does not surface _usage on its step output (follow-up)'.\n\nSo the undercount this ticket exists to fix is still live on the review-bot/CloudWatch path. Remaining work: mirror the plan-review aggregation into code_review/batch_runner.py so its batch step output carries _usage, and extend _attach_code_review_metrics (and delete the stale comment at finalize.py:139-141) with a code-review finalize unit test.\n\nLeaving this ticket OPEN. No --force / --force-close was used."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786087071869748001,"uuid":"c7a65b67-fb2d-4d05-b565-96490b1115ba"}